# DB + services target: Docker on a LAN host — use that host's LAN name/IP or compose service name (see docs/INFRA-BASELINE.md).
# Nest may also load `.env.development.local`, `.env.local`, `.env.development` (override order → see `app.module.ts`). Prisma `db:*` scripts use this file for `DATABASE_URL` unless you merge env another way.
DATABASE_URL="mysql://USER:PASSWORD@db-host.example:3306/ganhealth"
PORT=3000
JWT_SECRET="your-jwt-secret"